/// Memory management for Miri: copying a value, and moving one out of a place.
///
/// Defines the Cloneable trait for types that support deep copying, and
/// `replace`, the one way ownership of a value leaves a place.
///
/// Types implementing `Cloneable` guarantee that `clone()` returns an
/// independent copy: mutations to the original do not affect the clone
/// and vice versa.

@element("place, new")
@writes("place")
@stores("new")
@returns_element
runtime "core" fn miri_rt_replace<T>(place out T, new T) T

/// Enables creating a deep copy of a value.
///
/// The returned clone is fully independent of the original.
/// Managed fields (String, List, Array, Set, Map) are recursively cloned;
/// primitive fields (int, bool, float) are bitwise-copied.
///
/// A collection copies its elements through their `clone`: `clone()`,
/// `filter`, `resize` and `push_copy` call it once per element they copy, so
/// each copy of a class with a `drop` hook is its own value and runs its own
/// hook. A collection of such a class that does not implement `Cloneable`
/// cannot be copied: the call is refused where the program makes it.
///
/// Example:
///     use system.memory
///     let a = "hello"
///     let b = a.clone()   // b is a separate copy
///
/// `@copy_trait` makes this the trait a copy calls `clone` through; the
/// compiler finds it by the marker, never by its name, and a program never
/// needs to write it.
@copy_trait
public trait Cloneable
    public fn clone() Self

/// Puts `new` in `place` and returns the value `place` held, in one step.
///
/// The value returned is the caller's own: reading a value out of a place
/// only borrows it, and `replace` is how it leaves the place instead. The
/// place is never empty, and no value is copied: a value with a `drop` hook
/// runs it once, where the returned value ends.
///
/// Example:
///     use system.memory
///     var name = "old"
///     let previous = replace(name, "new")
///     println(f"{previous} {name}")   // old new
public fn replace<T>(place out T, new T) T
    return miri_rt_replace(place, new)
